@@ -47,6 +47,10 @@ You can find our backwards-compatibility policy [here](https://github.com/hynek/
 
   [#675](https://github.com/hynek/structlog/pull/675)
 
+- Logging an exception outside of an exception handler (for example, by calling `log.exception()` without an active exception) does not render a bogus `exception` key anymore.
+  This applies to `structlog.processors.format_exc_info`, `structlog.processors.dict_tracebacks`, and `structlog.processors.ExceptionRenderer` in general, as well as `structlog.processors.ExceptionPrettyPrinter` and `structlog.dev.ConsoleRenderer`.
+  Previously, it resulted in `"MISSING"` or an empty list, respectively.
+
 
 ## [24.4.0](https://github.com/hynek/structlog/compare/24.3.0...24.4.0) - 2024-07-17
 
